    "proof": "Evenness and real coefficients give J_m(i)=sum a_r(-1)^r in R. Because i^(2m+2)=(-1)^(m+1), the chosen c makes the added term equal -J_m(i) at i; evenness gives the root -i. The coefficient change starts only at degree 2m+2. Rouche's theorem supplies the positive bridge once a strict uniform tail inequality is proved on a contour.",
